          <msContents>
            <summary>Livre de receptes exprouveés [sic]. A collection of receipts by Ferrand and others written in the first half of the 16th cent., together with others by later hands, down to 1671: in French and Latin. 
              Other receipts by other hands are dated: fol. xviii, 1602; fol. xxvv, 1604; fol. ii, 1638; fol. xxviv, 1666; fol. xxvii, 1668; fol. xxviiv, 1671. 
              The earliest dated receipt is on fol. xvi: 'Recepte pour le mal de la Ratière composée par messire ferrand le ve de décembre M Vc XV'. 
              Another on fol. xix reads: 'Ordonnance faicte pour moy par monsieur maître Jacques ferrand en mois d'auril mil cinqcens trentequatre'.
              On the last two leaves are notes by the original compiler, dated 1550, giving details of the engagement and salaries of servants.</summary>
            <textLang mainLang="fr" source="IANA">French</textLang>
            <msItem n="1" xml:id="MS_271_1">
